            %p
              We discuss the first case, the second is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Cyl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \colon Cyl(X) \longrightarrow Y
              be the given left homotopy. By lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GoodCylinderObjectsSupportEveryLeftHomotopyAndDually"}
              we may assume without restriction that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cyl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cyl(X)
              is
              %em good
              in the sense of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PathAndCylinderObjectsInAModelCategory"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComponentsOfGoodCylinderOfCofibrantAreAcyclicCofibrationsAndDually"}
              implies that we have a lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              in the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
